-- check/bad: the shortest shape of `language.md` §7's top-level
-- initialisation rule. A top-level value is computed once, when the module
-- loads, so its own result cannot be part of computing it: `cyclic_value`,
-- with nothing in between and a one-name circle.
--
-- Until queue slice 23 this checked clean, built with exit 0 and emitted
-- `const CyclicValueSelf$x = Basics$add(CyclicValueSelf$x, 1);`, which throws
-- `ReferenceError: Cannot access 'CyclicValueSelf$x' before initialization`
-- the moment Node loads the module.
pub x : Int
x =
    x + 1
